        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThis is an [intended behavior](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/8dccba88fc4dce006ca0ad668067c9e0d5ce7702/doc/mini-ai.txt#L173-L179) for all non-Latin characters that are not part of special symbols (like `\"`, `'`, etc.). The logic is to primarily work for cases like pressing `da_` in `aaa_bbb_ccc` with cursor on `b` leads to `aaa_ccc` (i.e. deletes only one of separators). This is initially taken from 'wellle/targets.vim' and I think it makes sense.\n\nFor specific identifiers to include both left and right characters in \"a\" textobject, there needs to be explicit configuration (either in `require('mini.ai').setup()` or in buffer-local `vim.b.miniai_config`). So something like this:\n\n```lua\nrequire('mini.ai').setup({\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    ['*'] = { '%*().-()%*' },\n  },\n})\n```",
